@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Compact P1 parking hall — 2026-10-23
+
+The owner found the first hall too large and lacking the character of a parking garage. This revision replaces its open proving-ground layout with a 120 × 72 m P1 basement, 77.5% less floor area. The mode still offers free, untimed driving with the existing five cars and controls.
+
+| Requirement | Delivered behaviour |
+| --- | --- |
+| GPC01 | Compact local facility v2, 90 m clear aisle run and 12 m clear manoeuvring radius. Shared authored wall/column geometry and solid parked-car capsules. Existing handling/camera/records rules remain. |
+| GPC02 | North Garage/P1 identity; muted teal A and brick-red B bands; numbered perimeter/central parking banks; three static existing car models; pedestrian crossing; stair door, wall-mounted exit signs and shutter; fire cabinets, wall vents and wall service pipes. |
+| GPC03 | The owner's screenshot feedback explicitly removes roof/ceiling, overhead beams, ducts and fixtures. The unused ceiling shader and presentation updater are removed. Floor arrows use a solid head/shaft, corrected winding and two-sided paint, with the south aisle pointing east and the north aisle west. |
+| GPH01–GPH04 / R01 / G01 / Q01 | Retain Garage entry/reset/pause/background/return, saved cosmetics and unchanged PB/condition. Isolated local evidence, scoped patch and explicit owner/device limits. |
+
+The solid geometry lives in `game/garage/parking_hall_data.gd`. Twenty-four round column bounds are also used by the renderer. Three parked cars reuse the existing Compact, Pickup and Classic models in static simplified form; two overlapping circles per car form conservative rounded collision capsules. Paint, arrows, cones and service details are presentation only. The facility identity changes to `garage-parking-hall-v2`; shared physics, race rules and server track formats do not change.
+
+The visual builder batches repeated fixtures by material and merges compatible static cylindrical/car parts. An original floor shader supplies restrained concrete joints/wear, epoxy parking zones and soft light pools. No generated bitmap, downloaded asset, network media service, new dependency or dynamic light per space is introduced.
+
+The focused native harness covers all five cars, real pointer/touch entry, saved cosmetic parts/paint, acceleration, all four enclosing walls, swept columns and parked cars, a clear manoeuvring area, reset/pause/background input release and retained Garage return. It retains the original no-proof/no-ticket/no-PB/no-condition-write checks. Screenshots use the ordinary gameplay camera at entry, manoeuvring space, slalom, bays and stairs, across three landscape window sizes in Compatibility and desktop Mobile/Vulkan.
+
+The initial revised hall passed423 headless and445 Compatibility checks. Native review then centred parked cars inside their spaces and moved the stair capture clear of a column. The owner rejected the arrows and ceiling in a supplied screenshot. Roof/ceiling construction and its shader/updater were removed, hanging signs moved to the walls, and the floor-arrow geometry, winding and direction were corrected. Native image probes now compare arrow paint against adjacent concrete so invisible/cull-rejected triangles cannot pass unnoticed. Earlier ceiling comparisons are retained only as superseded evidence. Initial images/logs and the rejected ceiling source are preserved. Final results, commands, hashes and checkpoint validation are recorded in [report.json](evidence/parking-hall-character-2026-10-23/report.json). The reproducible runner is retained beside that report.
+
+Restart the local client to load the revision. Owner size, atmosphere and driving-feel acceptance remains. Phone/tablet attachment was not checked; no physical-device test, APK export/install, live backend/account mutation or deployment was performed. Desktop renderer checks are not mobile FPS, memory or thermal measurements. Concurrent workspace work and earlier evidence are preserved.
